     dropped and Burke's AGN variability lecture moves here from Day 4 to
     fill 11:45–13:00 (as a lecture, not the discussion it was on Day 4).
     r-process nucleosynthesis is dropped entirely, and so — in a second pass
     the same day — are kilonovae and neutrino astrophysics, whose two slots
     become KMB Asad's hour on TART, the Transient Array Radio Telescope (the
     one session that links out to /research/tart). Gap transients keeps the
     15:30 half-hour, so the afternoon still ends at 16:00 and frees 16:15 for
     Md Redyan Ahmed's new "Introduction to Exoplanet Science". Miller runs the
     17:00 lab.
   · Day 3 — the two TESS sessions (mission, follow-up programmes) are
     dropped and KMB Asad's "Pulsars in the Time Domain" takes 11:45–13:00.
     The 16:15 ground-based follow-up lecture and the 17:00 TESS lab merge
     into a single 16:15–18:00 hands-on, Uddin with TA M. S. H. Shahal.
   · Day 4 — AGN variability having moved to Day 2, Asad's FRB lecture grows
     to 11:45–13:00. Core-collapse SNe comes back up to 15:15, and the
     real-time-pipelines lecture merges with the ML lab into one 16:15–18:00
     hands-on, Uddin with TA A. Imtiaz. The gamma-ray lecture is Dipen
     Bhattacharya's (online), matching his field.
