/* ── People: invited speakers (full-width, prominent) + the two committees ──
   web: each speaker's public page — CASSA profiles for Uddin and Asad,
   personal / institutional sites otherwise (Miller's from his email
   signature). Photos for Miller and Ghosh fetched from those sites
   (2026-07-14); the rest reuse the people-collection portraits.
   Burke added 2026-08-09 (user) — the printed A5 brochure lists seven resource
   people and the page had six. Title/affiliation from his Yale listing and
   personal site, portrait cropped from the full-length photo there (the
   brochure's own thumbnail is only 100px). He sits after the IUB faculty and
   before Ahmed, matching both the seniority order used here and the brochure's
   Burke→Ahmed adjacency.
   Jewel Kumar Ghosh replaced by Payaswini Saikia (user, 2026-08-28); she takes
   his slot in the list and his sentence in the About lede. Her details come
   from her own people-collection entry (src/content/people/saikia.md), so her
   card links to the CASSA profile rather than out.
   M Arshad Momen removed 2026-09-01 (user, from SA Uddin's PDF markup) — off
   the page entirely: this list, the About lede and the neutrino session's
   speaker line. These cards are now the ONLY place affiliations and CASSA
   memberships appear; the lede names each speaker's subject, not their
   institution, so the two never drift out of sync.
   Dipen Bhattacharya added 2026-09-05 (user). The only source given was his
   Daily Star author page, which is therefore what his card links to and where
   the affiliation and portrait come from (cropped square from the full-res
   author avatar there). That bio is written in the past tense — "later worked
   as a gamma-ray astronomer at UC Riverside, while also teaching physics at
   Moreno Valley College" — so this card states his field and those two
   institutions rather than a current title, which the source does not give.
   No email is published there, so his card shows none (the render already
   treats email as optional; the field is "" to keep the array's type uniform).
   He sits after the IUB faculty and before Saikia on the seniority order used
   here (PhD 1990), and takes the matching position in the About lede — after
   Asad, before Burke (user, 2026-09-05). His lede sentence stays inside what
